# Exp. 1 (c) c_fjord3d -- case ${case}
# Eastern open boundary (fjord mouth) at column Nx-1 (OB_Ieast=-2,
# pkg/obcs/obcs_readparms.F:671-672); column Nx is land and closes the
# periodic x-wrap, as in (a), (b). Given for all Ny rows incl. land rows.
# WHY NOT ORLANSKI (task-7 fix, brief task-7-fix-stevens-c-brief.md): the 1-day
# timed run c_fjord_all_short1d (2 stages of 12 h, np=5, dt=60 s) ended OK but
# the Orlanski OB drained the domain: domain-mean eta -3.03 m at 12 h and
# -11.38 m at 24 h, OB transport obc_E_uVel_Int = +28,900 then +58,300 m3/s
# (outflow) against a net source Q0_total = 100 m3/s (sum addMass/rho0 = Q0).
# Orlanski leaves the depth-mean normal velocity free. Esteban approved
# Stevens on 2026-11-05, as already done for (b).
# STEVENS: the depth-mean normal velocity is PRESCRIBED from OBEu.bin and the
# baroclinic part (previous-step boundary u minus its depth mean) is kept
# (pkg/obcs/obcs_calc_stevens.F:195-228, header lines 19-44); T and S are
# advected out with a phase speed and restored toward OBEt/OBEs on
# TrelaxStevens/SrelaxStevens (same file, OBCS_STEVENS_CALC_TRACER_EAST).
# OBEu.bin = Q0_total/A_ob eastward on wet OB faces (gendata/make_case.py,
# _stevens_east; ob_u_m_per_s, ob_area_m2 in case.json) so the discharge
# leaves exactly; OBEv = 0. OBEt/OBEs keep carrying the time-varying shelf
# forcing (records every externForcingPeriod, cycle = shelf period; Sermilik
# profile with the pycnocline heaved by A sin(2 pi t/P), A = 30 m, P = 6 d,
# Jackson et al. 2018; non-shelf cases: the initial profile, constant records).
# Because (c) uses periodicExternalForcing, pkg/obcs reads EVERY OB file with
# the periodic record logic (pkg/obcs/obcs_fields_load.F:102-105, 159-173), so
# OBEu/OBEv have the same number of records as OBEt/OBEs (all identical).
# TrelaxStevens = SrelaxStevens = 86400 s: MITgcm verification/exp4/
# input.stevens/data.obcs value.
# KNOWN COST: the barotropic mode is closed at the OB (the depth-mean u is
# fixed at Q0/A_ob), so there is no wind-setup exchange of volume with the
# shelf; the baroclinic exchange (u minus its depth mean) is free.
# Restart: Stevens writes/reads pickup_stevensE.<iter> (pkg/obcs/
# obcs_write_pickup.F:225-231, obcs_read_pickup.F:241-246), see run_campaign.py.
# T/S sponge (10 cells = 2 km) relaxes toward the OB values: the
# relaxation zone of Cowton et al. 2015 (Sec. 3.2), here time dependent.
# No useOBCSbalance: it ignores addMass (obcs_balance_flow.F:300-315).
# OBCS_monitorFreq: obc_E_uVel_Int (area-integrated OB transport [m3 s-1],
# obcs_monitor.F:262-263) is printed to STDOUT every hour; compare with Q0_total.
 &OBCS_PARM01
 OB_Ieast=${ny}*-2,
 useOrlanskiEast=.FALSE.,
 useStevensEast=.TRUE.,
 useOBCSprescribe=.TRUE.,
 OBEuFile='OBEu.bin',
 OBEvFile='OBEv.bin',
 OBEtFile='OBEt.bin',
 OBEsFile='OBEs.bin',
 useOBCSsponge=.TRUE.,
 OBCSsponge_Theta=.TRUE.,
 OBCSsponge_Salt=.TRUE.,
 OBCS_monitorFreq=3600.,
 &

 &OBCS_PARM03
# relaxation time 600 s at the OB, 6 h at the inner edge (both << 6 d);
# the T/S sponge uses the U timescales (obcs_sponge.F:553-559)
 spongeThickness=10,
 Urelaxobcsinner=21600.,
 Vrelaxobcsinner=21600.,
 Urelaxobcsbound=600.,
 Vrelaxobcsbound=600.,
 &

 &OBCS_PARM04
 TrelaxStevens=86400.,
 SrelaxStevens=86400.,
 &
